        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'Go back to Mama Chebet's three containers. What have we answered, and what do we still not know about the bucket?' Give WAIT TIME of 10 seconds. Cold-call 3 groups to read a new question aloud and say which evidence prompted it. Ask: 'Mr. Kiprop asks why his bucket is not as big as the drum. Which question on our board helps us with that?' Point out that the pyramid is a stepping stone toward the frustum. Cluster questions and mark 'Lesson 4: frustum of a cone' next to the bucket question. Do not answer frustum questions yet.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Question-driven learning with a public record: the DQB tracks what the class now knows and what it still needs, motivating the next lessons and giving learners ownership of the inquiry path toward the bucket.",
        "formativeAssessment": "Observable indicators: each group posts at least one new, relevant question; at least one question links to the frustum or the bucket; questions are sorted correctly; learners can name the evidence that answered an old question. Teacher records which groups ask only recall questions versus extension questions."
