    "teacherReflection": "Did learners level their pours and measure perpendicular height rather than slant height? How many cited the Lesson 2 one-third idea in their predictions, and did their ideas change after the pour? Which learners confused volume (cm³) with capacity (L)? Did the new DQB questions point toward the frustum bucket? Plan to revisit any learners using slant height or calculating base area incorrectly before Lesson 4, and consider more sand or grain if pours were messy.",
