      "purposeInStoryline": "This is the culmination of the storyline. Learners return to Mama Chebet's drum (A), cover (B) and bucket (C) in Kericho and bring together everything gathered in Lessons 1-7: the pouring evidence for one third, the pyramid, the large-minus-small method for frustums, the problem solving and the project models. They complete the DQB, compare their Lesson 1 predictions with the real values, finish the cumulative model as one annotated diagram, and show what they can now do independently in a written class activity.",
      "safetyNotes": "Keep floors dry; wipe up any spilled water from the project verification immediately to prevent slipping. Learners handle the model containers, scissors and rulers carefully. Tidy and reuse card, sand and containers from the project. Carry water containers in pairs. Nobody is to taste any water or materials used in the models."
