    "overview": "Ms. Wanjiru opens by reminding learners of Mr. Kiprop's question at the Kericho weighing station: why is the bucket not as big as the drum when they look the same size? Over three 40-minute periods, learners (1) present their Lesson 7 project models, with calculated versus measured capacities and explanations of error, (2) revisit their Lesson 1 predictions and the DQB, and build the final class diagram that shows the cylinder (83.16 L) as exactly 3 x the cone (27.72 L), the bucket (58.52 L) as large cone (83,160 cm3) minus small cone (24,640 cm3), and the pyramid and its frustum following the same one-third and large-minus-small ideas, (3) write their Final Explanation of the phenomenon, and (4) complete a written class activity covering all five specific learning outcomes. This lesson does not teach new content; it consolidates and assesses.",
